The function at CS:0da7 load_page_b_w/_ptr load either of: castle, sektor, backup, demofile.
They are all in the same format
the first 40 bytes are always identical, 100 bytes are identical up to few variables

hence room_page always refer to a page of the same format
I'll call it castle_page and the function load_castle_page_w/_ptr

the castle pages are devided to pages. the first page contain various data about the game state. 
the next 38 pages are identical in format and represent rooms in the castle. 
The last page, which is C bytes short- unclear.
The data page is loaded to castle_page, the current room data is loaded to room_page. 


size is 3FF4

040: room_id 
     room page ordinal
041: movemnt direction  #bitmapped 0000 ><^v
042: aiming direction   #bitmapped 0000 ><^v
043: tile position of player    #error_id - 40
044: x-coordinate of player in the room     
045: y-coordinate of player in the room
046: isTransition
047: number bullets
048: number of granades.
049: uniform
04a: vest
04b: aim (alchohol decrese)
04c: bonk timer
04d: room timer
04f: rooms visited
051: action timer
052: isLooting
053: paragraph array index
059: bitmapped keys
06c: has_plans 
    if non-zero increment rank_index towards 0xf0 twich
06d: rank_index
06f: Game status: 
    0 ongoing, resuming 
    1..80 Game Overed, loading from backup
        40 Caught
        50 killed
        60 suicide
    80..ff error, creating new file
    ff win, creating new file


